prompt:
Your friend Jim is moving furniture this weekend. He originally asked you to help and you're writing an email to explain why you can't help. You should write between 80 and 120 words. You should include the following reasons:
• work;
• transport;
• family.

You are renting an apartment, but there are some problems with it. Your neighbors are noisy, and the hot water system hasn't been working properly. This isn't the first time you've had problems with the hot water system. Write an email to Marvin, the owner of the building, explaining the situation and asking him to resolve these issues. You should write between 80 and 120 words. You should include:
• What problems you have encountered;
• How you are affected;
• How to fix the problems.

You are going to give a presentation at your friend Jim's company, but you are not familiar with the venue, so you are writing to ask about some basic information. You should write between 80 and 120 words. Your ideas must come from the following three themes:
• Describe your situation, including the exact time;
• Ask about the availability of technology equipment, such as computers and projectors;
• Ask about the number of participants.

You and your friends went shopping and then had dinner at a restaurant yesterday. You think you left a bag at the restaurant. You tried to call them, but they did not answer your phone. Write an email to the restaurant manager. You should write between 80 and 120 words. Your ideas must come from the following three themes:
• Describe your situation: who you were with, where you sat, etc.;
• What the bag looks like and what was in the bag;
• Ask them to contact you.

You live on the second floor of an apartment building with no elevator. There is only one dim light at the entrance of the building, and there is no light by the stairs. Please write an email to Mr. Jackson describing the difficulties mentioned above. You should write between 80 and 120 words. Your email should cover the following three points:
• Install more lights;
• Install brighter lights;
• Install motion-sensing lighting.

Susan has invited you to go to a movie with her on Tuesday evening, but you can't go that time. Write a letter to explain why you can't go. You should write between 80 and 120 words. You should include:
• Thank for her invitation;
• Apologize for it;
• Suggest another time to go.

As a parent, you write an email to other parents and invite their children to take part in your son Alex's birthday party. You should write between 80 and 120 words. Your email should include the following three themes:
• When and where the party will be held;
• What food will be served;
• What activities will be arranged.

You are writing to ask the restaurant manager if you can reserve a table in Oscar's kitchen for a friend to hold a birthday party for twenty people next Friday, because you can only book a table for six people online. You should write between 80 and 120 words. Your ideas must come from the following three themes:
• Time;
• Details;
• Parking.

Write an email to your neighbor who has just moved in and ask him/her to address some issues. You should write between 80 and 120 words. The issues mentioned in the email should include the following three words:
• Noise;
• Parking;
• Garbage.

You need to take a vacation for 2 weeks. Your manager Dani wants you to send her an email with all the details. You should write between 80 and 120 words. You should include:
• Exact dates of the vacation;
• Reasons for the leave;
• Who will cover for you during that time and how can they reach you, if they have to.

Your company is trying to save energy, and you want to write an email to make some suggestions to the manager Mrs Smith about energy reduction. You should write between 80 and 120 words. Your ideas must come from the following three themes:
• Turning off the lights;
• Shutting down computers;
• Heating and air-conditioning.

You are helping your friend, Mrs. Singh, organize a party. She has asked you to send her an email suggesting ways to make the event enjoyable and memorable for all guests. You should write between 80 and 120 words. Your ideas must come from the following three themes:
• Music;
• Food;
• Activities.
